      "message": "[error] Line 2287: 🔴 `AccountManager::startSync` invokes this callback even when the permanent `put` completes with `ok \u003d\u003d false` (account_manager.cpp:302-309); that failure is expected to be retried when the DHT reconnects. `exchange(true)` therefore marks the device as announced and suppresses the later successful callback. If the transient failure does not produce a registration-state transition, this connection never bootstraps its conversations and the volatile detail is also reported as true. Propagate the put result and consume the one-shot guard only after a successful announcement, while preserving retries.",
